[38;5;231m⏺[39m Last question, then I'll write up the design.

  [1mFourth question — how do other forms reach the stored ID?[0m Right now there's no mechanism: [38;5;153mindex.html:13[39m loads [38;5;153mapp.js[39m
  as a plain [38;5;153m<script>[39m, and [38;5;153mlogin[39m/[38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m are bare globals. "Works across the app" needs something that doesn't
  exist yet, and this choice sets the pattern every future form follows.

  - [1mNew [38;5;153msession.js[39m, loaded as a plain [38;5;153m<script>[39m before [38;5;153mapp.js[0m, exposing a small [38;5;153mSession[39m object with [38;5;153mgetUserId()[39m /
    [38;5;153msetUserId()[39m / [38;5;153mclear()[39m. Matches the existing style exactly, needs no tooling, and [38;5;153mindex.html[39m opens straight from the
    filesystem as it does today. Cost: one more global, which is what this codebase already does everywhere.
  - [1mConvert to ES modules[0m — [38;5;153m<script type="module">[39m, [38;5;153msession.js[39m exports, [38;5;153mapp.js[39m imports. No globals, proper dependency
    edges, better long-term. Two real costs: it changes how [38;5;153mapp.js[39m loads, and ES modules are blocked by CORS over
    [38;5;153mfile://[39m, so you'd need a local web server to open the page at all. That's a workflow change for a repo that
    currently needs none.
  - [1mInline it in [38;5;153mapp.js[0m — no new file, but then every future form has to load the file containing the login form
    handler. It fails the "other forms will need it" requirement you started with.

  I recommend [38;5;153msession.js[39m as a plain script. It's the option that matches the code that's already here, and if you later
  adopt modules or a bundler, a single well-bounded file with three functions is the easiest possible thing to convert.
